# Mobile Responsive UI

Seraphova uses custom CSS in `app/globals.css` — no Tailwind.

## Breakpoints

| Token | Value | Use |
|-------|-------|-----|
| `--bp-tablet` | 1024px | Sidebars → drawers; inline columns collapse |
| `--bp-mobile` | 768px | Grids stack, reduced padding, typography tweaks |

- `@media (max-width: 1024px)` — drawer behavior (tablet + phone)
- `@media (max-width: 768px)` — layout stacking

## Sidebars & Drawers

1. **No persistent side columns below 1024px** — use off-canvas drawers with backdrop overlay.
2. Close drawers on: backdrop tap, Escape key, navigation (link click).
3. Lock body scroll when any drawer is open: `document.body.style.overflow = 'hidden'`.
4. Reuse shared classes: `.drawer-backdrop`, `.drawer`, `.drawer.open`, `.nav-burger`, `.burger-icon`.

## Two burger menus on chat

- **AppNav burger** (nav bar): Chat / Today / People / Profile / Sign out
- **Chat header burger**: conversations, New conversation, Daily briefing, Relationships

## Touch & spacing

- Interactive controls ≥ 44×44px on mobile.
- Content padding: 16px mobile, 24–28px desktop.
- Message bubbles: ~85–90% max-width on mobile.

## Layout rules

- Grids stack to 1 column at 768px: `.ob-row`, `.choice-grid`, `.plans`, `.comparison`.
- Use `100dvh` (not `100vh`) for full-viewport shells (`.app`, landing hero).
- No horizontal overflow — stack or `overflow-x: auto`, never clip off-screen.

## Scope

Drawer open/close is local React state only — no new routes, APIs, or features.
